--TEST--
`Core\IO::open` is the one member whose capability its argument decides: `Read` shows `fs.read`, `Write` shows `fs.write`, and `ReadWrite` shows both — so the same path opens under one mode and is refused under another — `rule:security/capability-question-is-grant-and-scope` and `rule:security/capability-check-at-the-door`, spec § 14
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The grant below reads everything here and writes only `scratch`. A door that
// asked one fixed capability for this member would have to pick, and either
// answer is wrong for half the modes.
Core\IO\File $in = Core\IO::open("note.txt", Core\IO\FileMode::Read);
echo "read: ", $in->read(5), "\n";
$in->close();

// Same path, different mode, different answer. The refusal is a catchable
// RuntimeError and arrives before anything is created -- which is the whole
// reason the check is inside the door rather than after the open.
try {
    Core\IO\File $never = Core\IO::open("note.txt", Core\IO\FileMode::Write);
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
    echo "write outside the grant: refused\n";
}

// Inside the write grant it opens, and the file it creates is the one the
// program named.
Core\IO\File $out = Core\IO::open("scratch/new.txt", Core\IO\FileMode::Write);
uint $wrote = $out->write("in scope\n");
echo "wrote ", $wrote as string, " bytes\n";
$out->close();

// `ReadWrite` needs both, and both are granted here: `read` covers the whole
// tree and `write` covers this subtree. A handle that can do either is a
// handle that can do both, so it shows both rather than the weaker one.
Core\IO\File $both = Core\IO::open("scratch/new.txt", Core\IO\FileMode::ReadWrite);
echo "read-write: ", $both->read(64);
$both->close();

// And the read-only half of the tree refuses it, because one of the two
// capabilities it needs is missing.
try {
    Core\IO\File $nor = Core\IO::open("note.txt", Core\IO\FileMode::ReadWrite);
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
    echo "read-write outside the grant: refused\n";
}
--FILE note.txt--
hello world
--FILE scratch/keep.txt--
keep
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.fs]
read = ["."]
write = ["scratch"]
--EXPECT--
read: hello
write outside the grant: refused
wrote 9 bytes
read-write: in scope
read-write outside the grant: refused
